@startuml
title Amend the contract and answer on a moved state

actor Owner
participant "avarice contract amend" as Amend
participant "avarice decide" as Decide
database Ledger
participant Supervisor

note over Ledger : contract version 1 is in force.\nDecision A (a repeated failure, answered by an amendment) and\ndecision B (a pause with choices) are open, both stamped with\nthe digest of version 1.

== The amendment ==
Owner -> Amend : amend with a reason, a budget or write change, and decision A
alt inside a run, no terminal, or from a run's process tree
  Amend --> Owner : refused (64), before the profile is resolved
end
Amend -> Ledger : read the run, its latest contract, the evidence and gate rows
alt run failed, cancelled or closed, decision A not open or not of an amendable class\n(repeated failure, permission, budget or scope expansion),\nrequest empty, a field not amendable, or static gate G0 fails
  Amend --> Owner : refused, nothing written
end
Amend -> Amend : build version 2: field diff, what it invalidates,\nwhich evidence and gates get a stale copy
Amend --> Owner : preview of the diff, the invalidations and the decision it answers
Owner -> Amend : apply version 2? y or n
alt n or no answer
  Amend --> Owner : not amended (0)
else y
  Amend -> Ledger : one transaction without a lease: contract version 2 with diff, reason, owner;\nbudget limits changed, spend untouched; stale evidence and failed\nstale-after-amendment gate rows appended; decision A answered as amended:v2,\nits items released
  note over Ledger : refused with nothing written if version 1 is no longer the latest,\nthe run has ended, or decision A is no longer open
  Amend -> Amend : write the contract file of version 2
  Amend --> Owner : version 2 recorded, decision A answered (0)
end

== The supervisor ==
alt a supervisor holds a live lease
  Supervisor -> Ledger : reads the latest contract at its next unit or block,\nand takes the released item next
else no live lease
  note over Amend : the amend command starts no supervisor itself.\nThe amend chain inside decide checks the pickup as an answer does;\notherwise resume continues a run blocked on an item decision\nonce an item is ready.
end

== A stale answer ==
Owner -> Decide : decide B with a choice
Decide -> Ledger : read B and the latest contract
Decide -> Decide : digest of version 2 is not the digest B was stamped with
Decide -> Ledger : B stale with the answer kept,\nB2 opened on the new state, supersedes B
Decide --> Owner : answer not applied, B2 asks the same question, answer B2 (3)
Owner -> Decide : decide B again
Decide --> Owner : refused: B was re-opened, answer B2 (3)
Owner -> Decide : decide B2 with a choice
Decide -> Decide : digest matches
Decide -> Ledger : B2 answered, its items released
Decide --> Owner : answered (0)
note over Decide, Ledger : a withdraw is the one answer applied whatever the digest says
@enduml
